# Text rules for Tibetan (rules/dz.weir has the same for Dzongkha, which writes it alike).

# A syllable ends at its tsheg (་), and the keyboard types one after each
# syllable from the strip; the last before a shad (། or ༎) has none, but
# after ང, where it stays (ཁང་།): typed before a shad, the tsheg gives way.
rule TshegGivesWay
let message "The tsheg before a shad gives way to it, but after ང: རོལ། and ཁང་།."
expr main (!"…ང" "་" ["།", "༎"])
let becomes "$1$3"
test "ཟས་རོལ་།" "ཟས་རོལ།"
test "དེ་རེད་༎" "དེ་རེད༎"
allows "ཁང་།"
allows "ང་།"
allows "རོལ།"
